@startuml
title From a Rholang Spec Value to a Target Artifact — What Needs a Rust Compiler, and What Does Not
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #334155

rectangle "**Authoring**" as A #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "Rholang spec value <latex>v</latex>\nmaps / lists / tuples / strings" as V #E0E7FF
  rectangle "<latex>\texttt{language!}</latex> Rust source <latex>s</latex>" as S #FEF3C7
}

rectangle "<latex>\mathcal{E}(v)</latex> — elaborator [Proposed]\npure, total-or-fail-closed" as EL #E0E7FF
rectangle "<latex>\texttt{syn::parse\_str}</latex> +\n<latex>\texttt{reconstruct\_language\_def}</latex> [Implemented]" as PA #FEF3C7
rectangle "**<latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>**" as LD #DBEAFE

rectangle "**Semantics lane — emits DATA**" as SEM #ECFDF5 {
  rectangle "<latex>\texttt{lower\_language\_def}</latex>\n<latex>\rightarrow \texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex> contracts" as L1 #DCFCE7
  rectangle "<latex>\texttt{rho\_net\_*}</latex> driver network\n+ set-automaton pattern DAG\n<latex>\rightarrow \texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex>" as L2 #DCFCE7
  rectangle "<latex>\texttt{NativeHandlerSpec}</latex> table\n<latex>\rightarrow</latex> system-process <latex>\texttt{Definition}</latex>s" as L3 #DCFCE7
}

rectangle "**Syntax lane — emits RUST SOURCE**" as SYN #FEF2F2 {
  rectangle "PraTTaIL / WPDA pipeline\n<latex>\texttt{run\_pipeline}</latex>\n<latex>\rightarrow</latex> a <latex>\texttt{String}</latex> of Rust,\nthen <latex>\texttt{parse::<TokenStream>()}</latex>" as P1 #FEE2E2
  rectangle "AST enums, freshness fns,\nmetadata, <latex>\texttt{Language}</latex> impl,\nproptest strategies" as P2 #FEE2E2
}

rectangle "**f1r3node Rho machine**\nRSpace + spatial matcher + reducer\n(cross-compiled once, per target)" as VM #BFDBFE
rectangle "<latex>\texttt{riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf}</latex>\nbare-metal image" as RV #C7D2FE
rectangle "<latex>\texttt{rustc}</latex>" as RUSTC #FCA5A5

V --> EL
S --> PA
EL --> LD
PA --> LD
LD --> L1
LD --> L2
LD --> L3
LD --> P1
LD --> P2

L1 --> VM : installed as data
L2 --> VM : installed as data
L3 --> VM : injected via <latex>\texttt{extra\_system\_processes}</latex>
P1 --> RUSTC
P2 --> RUSTC
RUSTC --> VM
VM --> RV : cross-compile

note bottom of SEM #ECFDF5
  **Already data.** A running node can install these
  from a spec value with no compiler in the loop.
end note

note bottom of SYN #FEF2F2
  **Still code.** <latex>\texttt{run\_pipeline}</latex>'s terminal step is
  <latex>\texttt{combined.parse::<TokenStream>()}</latex> over concatenated
  Rust source. Getting a *parser* for a spec authored
  at runtime is the one genuinely missing artifact —
  named as work item **W-4** in this FIPS.
end note

legend right
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#E0E7FF> | Proposed Rholang path |
  |<#FEF3C7> | Existing Rust path (retained) |
  |<#DBEAFE> | Shared specification datatype |
  |<#DCFCE7> | Generator emitting installable DATA |
  |<#FEE2E2> | Generator emitting Rust SOURCE |
  |<#FCA5A5> | Rust compiler dependency |
  |<#BFDBFE> | Runtime substrate |
endlegend
@enduml
